      "dom_id": "question-82665",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\,$ **If** you are sick, **then** you are not going to school.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If you are not going to school, then you are sick.\n- If you are not sick, then you are going to school.\n- If you are going to school, then you are not sick.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114550/assets/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-82665\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">1.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/252#12713\">Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"82665\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 2em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> <strong>If</strong> you are sick, <strong>then</strong> you are not going to school.</p>\n<p>Which of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  If you are not going to school, then you are sick. </li><li>  If you are not sick, then you are going to school. </li><li>  If you are going to school, then you are not sick. </li></ol></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sat, Oct 10th @ 11:01 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:15</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
