      "dom_id": "question-183281",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not summer, **then** you don't go to the beach.",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You don't go to the beach.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is summer.\n\n- $¬B:$ You go to the beach.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is summer, then you go to the beach.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
