      "dom_id": "question-183337",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** ${0}⊂{1,2,3},$ **then** $4>6.$",
      "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ ${0}⊂{1,2,3}.$\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $4>6.$\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$\n\n- $¬B:$ $4\\le 6.$\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $4\\le 6,$ then ${0}⊄{1,2,3}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
