      "dom_id": "question-183340",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\,$ **If** $-2\\in Z,$ **then** $5$ is prime.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If $-2\\notin Z,$ then $5$ is not prime.\n- If $5$ is prime, then $-2\\in Z.$\n- If $5$ is not prime, then $-2\\notin Z.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114550/assets/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
